// The 5 s limit for one test, and the tests allowed past it. test/slow-guard.mjs measures every
// test (its hooks included) and judges one over the limit that SLOW_TESTS does not list
// (slowTestFinding):
// - It fails the test when the machine is idle: under IDLE_LOAD_PER_CORE (0.5) of the 1-minute
//   load per core, read as the test ends, or a load that cannot be read. vitest's retry then runs
//   it once more, so a one-off spike passes and a test that is always slow fails.
// - It prints a `slow-test guard warning:` line instead when the machine is busy (0.5 per core
//   or more), since several stories' suites share one machine and a test is not slow because the
//   machine is busy.
// The limit is LIMIT_MS while the machine has a core per runnable process, and stretches with the
// load past that (load 36 on 18 cores gives 10 s); it never goes below LIMIT_MS.
// SLOW_TEST_LIMIT_MS sets an exact limit for a run instead, with no load excuse.
// SLOW_TEST_GUARD=report turns every failure into a warning that says the test fails npm test on
// an idle machine: for checks that must not fail on the guard alone. A plain `npm test` is strict.
//
// SLOW_TESTS maps a test's vitest fullName ("path/from/root.test.mjs > describe > test") to what
// it waits on. List a test only when the waiting is its point or cannot be cut. Never a workshop
// file: those must stay fast.

import os from 'node:os';

export const LIMIT_MS = 5000;

// Under this 1-minute load per core the machine counts as idle, and a slow test fails.
export const IDLE_LOAD_PER_CORE = 0.5;

// The start of every line the guard prints instead of failing.
export const GUARD_WARNING = 'slow-test guard warning:';

